From: greyoak111 <151205158+greyoak111@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:14:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 44/51] Save live captions as SRT with each recording and
 stream
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Final captions now carry when they were spoken, taken from the recognizer's
audio timeline. A recording's captions are saved next to it with the same
name; a stream's go to the recording folder as "直播字幕 <start>.srt".
Times count from the start of the recording, leaving out paused
stretches, or of the stream. Long sentences are split at punctuation.
Late captions are still collected for 2.5 s after a stop, and pending
files are written when LiveHime quits. A Captions-tab switch (on by
default) turns it off; the tab shows the saved file with a Finder link.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
